Har din ke liye ye batao ki aaj se peeche kitne lagataar din tak
stock ka price aaj ke price se chhota ya barabar raha.

Hum peeche dekh rahe hain ki kaun sa price aaj se chhota ya barabar hai,
👆 Dekhne me aisa lagta hai, par kaam actually ulta ho raha hai.
Question ka actual kaam kya hai? Hum peeche ye nahi dhoondh rahe:
“kaun sa chhota hai?”
Hum actually ye dhoondh rahe hain:
“peeche pehla kaun sa bada price mila?”
⚠️ Jaise hi bada price milta hai → STOP
Example Prices: [7, 2, 1, 2]
Aaj ka price = 2
Peeche check:

1 ≤ 2 ✅ (continue)
2 ≤ 2 ✅ (continue)
7 > 2 ❌ (STOP HERE)
👉 Yeh 7 kya hai?
3 peeche ke din + 1 aaj ka din = 4

🔹 Example Input
prices = [100, 80, 60, 70, 60, 75, 85]
Goal → Har price ka span calculate karna.

🔹 Step by Step Dry Run
Initialization
stack<int> st = [] → indices of prices jinka span abhi calculate nahi hua
vector<int> prices = []
day = -1 → kyunki next() me pehle hi day++ karenge, first day ka index 0 ho jaye
Day 0 → price = 100
day++ → day = 0
prices.push_back(100) → prices = [100]
Stack empty → while loop skip
if(st.empty()) → true → span = day + 1 = 0 + 1 = 1
Reason: Pehle koi price nahi tha → span sirf current day = 1
st.push(0) → st = [0]

Return 1
✅ Span array so far: [1]
Day 1 → price = 80
day++ → day = 1
prices.push_back(80) → prices = [100, 80]
Stack top = 0 → prices[0] = 100 > 80 → while loop skip
Stack not empty → span = day - st.top() = 1 - 0 = 1
Reason: Pehle se bada price mila → span sirf 1 din
st.push(1) → st = [0,1]
Return 1

✅ Span array so far: [1,1]

Day 2 → price = 60
day = 2
prices = [100,80,60]
Stack top = 1 → prices[1]=80 > 60 → skip while
Stack not empty → span = 2 - 1 = 1
st.push(2) → st = [0,1,2]
Return 1

✅ Span array so far: [1,1,1]

Day 3 → price = 70
day = 3
prices = [100,80,60,70]
Stack top = 2 → prices[2]=60 ≤ 70 → pop → st=[0,1]
Stack top = 1 → prices[1]=80 > 70 → stop popping
Stack not empty → span = day - st.top() = 3 - 1 = 2
Reason: Peeche consecutive chhote prices = 60, apna din = 1+1 → 2
st.push(3) → st = [0,1,3]
Return 2

✅ Span array so far: [1,1,1,2]
Day 4 → price = 60
day = 4
prices = [100,80,60,70,60]
Stack top = 3 → prices[3]=70 > 60 → skip while
Stack not empty → span = 4 - 3 = 1
st.push(4) → st = [0,1,3,4]
Return 1

✅ Span array so far: [1,1,1,2,1]
Day 5 → price = 75
day = 5
prices = [100,80,60,70,60,75]
Stack top = 4 → prices[4]=60 ≤ 75 → pop → st=[0,1,3]
Stack top = 3 → prices[3]=70 ≤ 75 → pop → st=[0,1]
Stack top = 1 → prices[1]=80 > 75 → stop
Stack not empty → span = 5 - 1 = 4
Reason: Peeche consecutive chhote prices = 60,70, apna din = total 4
st.push(5) → st=[0,1,5]
Return 4

✅ Span array so far: [1,1,1,2,1,4]
Day 6 → price = 85
day = 6
prices = [100,80,60,70,60,75,85]
Stack top = 5 → prices[5]=75 ≤ 85 → pop → st=[0,1]
Stack top = 1 → prices[1]=80 ≤ 85 → pop → st=[0]
Stack top = 0 → prices[0]=100 > 85 → stop
Stack not empty → span = 6 - 0 = 6
Reason: Peeche consecutive chhote prices = 80,75,60,70,60 + apna din = 6
st.push(6) → st=[0,6]
Return 6
✅ Final Span Array: [1,1,1,2,1,4,6]


class StockSpanner {
public:
    stack<int> st;         // stack me indices store karenge
    vector<int> prices;    // har din ka price store karne ke liye
    int day;               // current day number
    StockSpanner() {
        day = -1; // start from -1, taaki pehla din 0 ho
    }
    
    int next(int price) {
        day++;
        prices.push_back(price);

         // stack me indices hai jinke prices current se bade hone chahiye
        while (!st.empty() && prices[st.top()] <= price) {
            st.pop();
        }
        int span;
        if (st.empty()) {
            span = day + 1;   // sab din chhote nikle
        } else {
            span = day - st.top();  // difference of indices
        }

        st.push(day);  // current index dal do
        return span;
    }
};

